# Data Layer

Drizzle + PostgreSQL schema lives in `packages/db/src/schema.ts` (exported via `@repo/db` and `@repo/db/schema`); the client is `packages/db/src/index.ts` and config is `packages/db/drizzle.config.ts`. Inferred types like `Project` come from `typeof project.$inferSelect`.

## tRPC
Routers live in `packages/api/src/router/`, composed into `appRouter` in `packages/api/src/root.ts`. Procedure builders (`publicProcedure`, `protectedProcedure`) and `createTRPCContext` (which injects `session`, `headers`, `db`) are in `packages/api/src/trpc.ts`; RBAC builders are in `packages/api/src/middleware/rbac.ts`. Keep all DB access inside procedures — never query Drizzle from a component.

## Client data (TanStack Query)
The web app wires tRPC + React Query in `apps/web/src/trpc/providers.tsx` (`useTRPC`) and server-side prefetch in `apps/web/src/trpc/server.tsx` (`trpc`, `prefetch`, `HydrateClient`). Components call `useQuery(trpc.x.y.queryOptions())` / `useMutation(trpc.x.y.mutationOptions())` — see `apps/web/src/components/projects/project-table.tsx`. After mutations, invalidate with `queryClient.invalidateQueries(trpc.x.y.queryFilter())`.

`QueryBoundary` (`apps/web/src/components/query-boundary.tsx`) pairs Suspense with an error boundary; wrap suspense-driven sections in it.

## Forms (TanStack Form)
`useAppForm` is composed in `packages/ui/src/lib/form.ts` (`@repo/ui/lib/form`) with shuip field components (`InputField`, `SelectField`, etc.). See `apps/web/src/components/projects/project-form.tsx`: a Zod schema in `validators.onChange`, `form.AppField` per field, and `form.SubmitButton` inside `form.AppForm`.

## Palette search
The command palette (Ctrl+K, or the search field under the organization switcher) lists the pages the active organization lets the user open and finds projects and members through one tRPC procedure, `search.records` (`packages/api/src/router/search.ts`, a `protectedProcedure`). It returns `{ type, label, items: { id, title, subtitle, href }[] }[]`, and the palette (`apps/web/src/components/navigation/command-palette.tsx`) shows whatever groups come back, so it knows no record type.
- The pages are `useAllowedRoutes()` (`apps/web/src/lib/allowed-routes.ts`), the list the sidebar renders: each route that needs a permission is asked through `permissionQueryOptions` (`apps/web/src/hooks/use-permission.ts`, the key `usePermission` and `<Can>` share), so the palette never offers a page the sidebar hides.
- `SEARCHABLE_TYPES` in `packages/api/src/search.ts` is the one list of what can be found. An entry declares `canSearch`, `find` (the query, at most the `limit` it is given) and the `href` of each item. To make a new type searchable, add one entry; the palette needs no change.
- Every query is scoped to the active organization of the session (`activeOrganizationId`, read on the server, never sent by the browser), and a session without one finds nothing. A type the caller may not read gets no group and runs no query. Projects use the check of `project.list` (`hasPermission(headers, organizationId, 'project', 'read')` from `packages/api/src/middleware/rbac.ts`, which `permissionProcedure` calls too). Members use the check of `member.list`, which asks no permission, only membership of the active organization. A caller better-auth refuses finds nothing.
- A member has no page of their own, so a member item opens the members page (`/settings/members`); a project item opens `/projects/<id>`.
- The text is cut at `MAX_SEARCH_LENGTH` (100) when the input is read (`packages/api/src/search-query.ts`, which also holds `SEARCH_MIN_LENGTH` for the palette), trimmed, and nothing is searched under 2 characters. Each type returns at most `SEARCH_LIMIT_PER_TYPE` (5) items (`packages/api/src/search-engine.ts`).
- The match is `containsText` (`packages/api/src/text-match.ts`): plain text and case-insensitive, so `%` and `_` match themselves (`position(lower(text) in lower(column))`), never `LIKE`. It cannot use an index, so a search scans the organization's rows; that is accepted at this size.

## Adding a query/mutation
1. Add the procedure to the relevant router in `packages/api/src/router/`, validating input with Zod and gating with `permissionProcedure`.
2. (New router) register it in `packages/api/src/root.ts`.
3. In the UI, call it through `useTRPC()` with `queryOptions`/`mutationOptions`; invalidate affected queries on success.

